      <p>They are a continuous process with the crowd playing a key and critical role in self governance.</p>
      <p>The Electoral Commission Network has now made the political process <span class="bold-green">&ldquo;Gamified.&rdquo;</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <p>The leader boards are constantly changing, forcing the candidates to take charge constantly.</p>
      <p>When watchdog organizations identify activities that are not progressive, they reflect on the leader board.</p>
      <p>Decision-making is determined by the positions of the candidates on the leader board.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <p>Leaders can check in to locations and let their voters know how much they have or intend to equalize that space.</p>
      <p>Voters who earn &ldquo;influencer&rdquo; badges have greater power to be able to&nbsp; affect policies.</p>
